{title: My Hope Is Built on Nothing Less}
{artist: Edward Mote (1797-1874)}
{key: F}
{copyright: Public Domain}

{sov: Verse 1}
My [F]hope is built on [C]nothing less
Than [Bb]Jesus’ blood and [C]righteous[F]ness;
I [F]dare not trust the [C]sweetest frame,
But [Bb]wholly lean on [C]Jesus’ [F]name.
{eov}

{soc}
On [F]Christ, the solid [Bb]Rock, I stand,
All [F]other ground is [C]sinking sand,
All [Bb]other ground is [C]sinking [F]sand.
{eoc}

{sov: Verse 2}
When [F]darkness veils His [C]lovely face,
I [Bb]rest on His un[C]changing [F]grace;
In [F]every high and [C]stormy gale,
My [Bb]anchor holds with[C]in the [F]veil.
{eov}

{soc}
On [F]Christ, the solid [Bb]Rock, I stand,
All [F]other ground is [C]sinking sand,
All [Bb]other ground is [C]sinking [F]sand.
{eoc}

{sov: Verse 3}
His [F]oath, His covenant, [C]His blood,
Sup[Bb]port me in the [C]whelming [F]flood;
When [F]all around my [C]soul gives way,
He [Bb]then is all my [C]hope and [F]stay.
{eov}

{soc}
On [F]Christ, the solid [Bb]Rock, I stand,
All [F]other ground is [C]sinking sand,
All [Bb]other ground is [C]sinking [F]sand.
{eoc}

{sov: Verse 4}
When [F]He shall come with [C]trumpet sound,
O [Bb]may I then in [C]Him be [F]found,
Dressed [F]in His righteous[C]ness alone,
Fault[Bb]less to stand be[C]fore the [F]throne.
{eov}

{soc}
On [F]Christ, the solid [Bb]Rock, I stand,
All [F]other ground is [C]sinking sand,
All [Bb]other ground is [C]sinking [F]sand.
{eoc}
